.TH pickles-update 1 "October 6, 2025" "Pickles Update" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pickles-update, pupdate - a script to perform system updates on Pickles Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pickles-update
[
.B OPTIONS
]
.B pickles-update
.B -S
.I packages
.P
.B pupdate
[
.B OPTIONS
]
.B pupdate
.B -S
.I packages
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B pickles-update
script automates the process of updating a Pickles Linux system. It automatically detects the operating system, updates the package list, and upgrades all installed packages from official repositories and AUR.
.P
The script also provides an optional feature to rate and update the package mirrors for improved download speeds. After the update is complete, the user is prompted to reboot the system.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Display the script version.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display this help message.
.TP
.B \-m, \-mirrors
Rate mirrors before updating.
.TP
.B \-S \fIpackages\fR
Install packages (official or AUR).
.TP
.B \-y
Refresh package databases.
.TP
.B \-u
Upgrade packages.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet mode.
.TP
.B \-\-noconfirm
Do not ask for confirmation.
.P
If no options are provided, defaults to -Syu (update).
.SH EXAMPLES
To simply run a standard system update:
.P
.B pickles-update
.P
To update the system and also rate the mirrors beforehand:
.P
.B pickles-update -m
.P
To display the script's version:
.P
.B pickles-update -v
.P
To install packages:
.P
.B pickles-update -S package1 package2
.SH NOTES
.RS
.IP *
This script requires
.B rate-mirrors
,
.B git
,
.B curl
to be installed on the system.
.IP *
The script should not be run with
.B sudo
; it will use
.B sudo
as required.
.IP *
A reboot is often recommended after a significant system update to ensure all changes take effect.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR rate-mirrors (1)
